{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… it’s this crampy pain in the middle of my stomach. It’s been going on for a while, but got worse a few days ago. I can’t keep anything down except a little soup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And have you had any fever, blood in your stool, or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:18:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No blood. I did feel a little feverish, but not sure. My stomach just hurts and I keep throwing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:19:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We checked your blood sugar when you came in, and it was high. You also had a small acid buildup, which we call a modest anion gap. That’s common in uncontrolled diabetes. We’re starting IV fluids and insulin to help correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:20:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know my sugars have been high. I’ve been stressed. I’ve been using my mom’s pain pills to help with the stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:21:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you're allergic to morphine, so we won’t use that. But we’ll manage your pain safely. We also ordered a CT scan to check your abdomen. It showed some thickening in the colon, but it looks stable and not acute."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? The colon thing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:23:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s been there a while, so it’s not an emergency. But we do need to check it further. The GI team recommends a sigmoidoscopy as an outpatient to make sure it’s not colitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. I was supposed to get a stomach test before, but I never went."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:24:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a gastric emptying study. That’s still important. Given your diabetes and ongoing nausea, we think you might have gastroparesis — that’s when the stomach doesn’t empty properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why I feel full and sick all the time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And it’s common in people with long-standing diabetes. We’ll need that test to confirm. We also want a stool test for H. pylori, since you had it before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:27:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I don’t want to stay in the hospital long. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2124-01-28 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re focused on getting your blood sugar under control and keeping you hydrated. The nausea is improving with anti-nausea meds. But you’ll need to follow up on those tests after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are better today. The acid in your blood has cleared, and your sugars are coming down with the insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I still feel kind of shaky though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:02:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching that. It could be from the insulin or from not eating. We’re trying to get you to tolerate small sips. How’s your pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but not as bad. I’m just so anxious. I hate being in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The psychiatry team saw you yesterday. They think your anxiety is making things harder. They recommend starting mirtazapine at night for sleep and anxiety, and you can take Ativan up to three times a day as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on Celexa before. Did that help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They reviewed it and think it hasn’t been effective, so we’re stopping it. Mirtazapine might help more with both sleep and appetite."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2124-01-29 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2124-01-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine test came back. It showed mixed bacteria, but it’s likely contamination from skin or genital area, so we don’t think you have a UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2124-01-30 14:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2124-01-30 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for now. We’re focusing on your diabetes, stomach issues, and anxiety. Your blood pressure is a bit high too, but we’ll manage that with your regular meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2124-01-31 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. You’ve been off IV fluids since this morning and tolerating small amounts of food. Your pain is less, and you’re not vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2124-01-31 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2124-01-31 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’d like to keep you a bit longer to finish monitoring, but we understand you want to leave. The GI team wanted to do the gastric emptying study and sigmoidoscopy here, but we can arrange them as outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2124-01-31 10:03:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d rather do them outside. I just can’t stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2124-01-31 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll set that up. But it’s very important you schedule them soon. Gastroparesis and colon changes need to be checked properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2124-01-31 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I promise I’ll call. I don’t want to end up back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — your vitals are stable. You’ve been eating soft foods without vomiting. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue pantoprazole for stomach protection, ezetimibe for cholesterol, and your insulin. We’re adjusting your long-acting insulin to 8 units at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s lower than before. Why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:34:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your sugars were high but now are improving. We don’t want you going too low, especially if you’re not eating well. You’ll also take half a mirtazapine pill at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:35:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Ativan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:36:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one tablet up to three times a day for anxiety. But don’t take more than that. We also recommend following up with a psychiatrist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:37:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I need help. I’ve been struggling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Case management is helping set up appointments at Central Clinic. It might be easier for you to go to one place for all your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2124-02-01 09:39:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would help. I get confused with all the different doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. Your discharge papers are ready. You’re stable, no fever, and you’ve been eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go. What do I need to do next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "First, call your GI doctor to schedule the gastric emptying study and sigmoidoscopy. They’re important to understand your stomach and colon issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call today. I mean it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Also, take your new meds as directed. Watch your blood sugar closely. If you start vomiting again or your sugars go very high, come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:05:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel really anxious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the Ativan as needed, but also try to reach your counselor. We’ve set up a case manager to help you stay on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:07:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll do better this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2124-02-02 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Take care, and please follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2124-02-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave — are you feeling okay to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2124-02-02 10:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m feeling much better. Still a little nervous, but I’ll be okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2124-02-02 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. Remember, the Ativan is there if you need it. And call the clinic if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2124-02-02 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge instructions are in your packet. The key points are: schedule the GI tests, take your meds, and follow up with your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2124-02-02 12:00:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve already called the GI office. They’re mailing me the prep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2124-02-02 12:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. Keep that momentum. You’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2124-02-02 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your insulin again before you leave. Make sure you’re comfortable with the doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2124-02-02 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think I’ve got it. 8 units at night, and the fast-acting with meals based on my sugar and carbs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2124-02-02 14:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And use the sliding scale if your sugar is high. You’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2124-02-02 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your A1c was high at 9.7%. We know diabetes is hard to manage, especially with everything else going on. But controlling it helps prevent complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2124-02-02 15:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’ll try harder. I don’t want to lose my kidneys or go blind."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2124-02-02 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re already taking steps. That’s what matters. We believe you can do this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay safe, and call if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you have a ride home and someone to check on you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:30:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my sister’s picking me up and staying tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take it easy, and we’ll talk soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2124-02-02 16:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take these printed instructions with you. Call the clinic Monday to confirm your appointments."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2124-01-28 19:51:00",
    "admission_end": "2124-02-02 17:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with poorly controlled type 1 diabetes was admitted for abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and hyperglycemia with a modest anion gap, consistent with mild diabetic ketoacidosis. Her metabolic abnormalities resolved with IV fluids and insulin therapy. Persistent gastrointestinal symptoms led to a GI consultation, which recommended outpatient evaluation for suspected gastroparesis with a gastric emptying study and assessment of chronic colonic wall thickening via flexible sigmoidoscopy. The patient declined inpatient procedures and opted for discharge. Psychiatry evaluated her for anxiety and recommended switching from citalopram to mirtazapine and using as-needed Ativan. She was discharged home with stable vital signs, improved symptoms, and a plan to follow up on pending studies and mental health care. Case management arranged centralized outpatient care to improve adherence.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with other specified manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Volume depletion, unspecified",
      "Fever, unspecified",
      "Unspecified adjustment reaction",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health"
    ]
  }
}
